,"produced_mana":["C"],"released_at":"2025-08-01","toughness":null,"type_line":"Basic Land"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"Because Wastes is a basic land, you can include as many of them as you like in your Constructed decks.","oracle_id":"05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"In Limited events (including Sealed Deck and Booster Draft), Wastes must be in your card pool to be included in your deck. You can't add Wastes to your card pool in the same way that you can add other basic lands.","oracle_id":"05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Wastes is not a land type. If something asks you to name a land type, you can't choose Wastes.","oracle_id":"05d24b0c-904a-46b6-b42a-96a4d91a0dd4","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The cost-reduction ability of Animist's Might doesn't change its mana cost or mana value, only the total cost you pay. Specifically, the mana value of Animist's Might is always 3.","oracle_id":"4940783f-2534-41c1-b614-5dabb0dff405","published_at":"2023-05-12","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The controller of Vedalken Orrery can cast nonland artifact, creature, enchantment, and sorcery cards any time they could cast an instant. This includes on other players' turns and during the upkeep step, draw step, combat phase, and end step.","oracle_id":"60d640a4-032b-4279-ac75-8f200ca776fb","published_at":"2004-12-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This applies only to casting spells. It does not, for example, change when you may activate abilities that can only be activated \"any time you could cast a sorcery\".","oracle_id":"60d640a4-032b-4279-ac75-8f200ca776fb","published_at":"2010-06-15","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If Aerie Ouphes has no -1/-1 counters on it when you sacrifice it to activate its first ability, persist will return Aerie Ouphes to the battlefield with a -1/-1 counter on it before that ability resolves. The ability will check the power of Aerie Ouphes at the time you sacrificed it, not the power of the returned Aerie Ouphes (which is actually a new object with no relation to its previous existence).","oracle_id":"70cdd24a-8dc5-47b5-8729-9ebf486f4821","published_at":"2008-08-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a creature with persist stops being a creature, persist will still work.","oracle_id":"70cdd24a-8dc5-47b5-8729-9ebf486f4821","published_at":"2013-06-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a creature with persist that has +1/+1 counters on it receives enough -1/-1 counters to cause it to be destroyed by lethal damage or put into its owner’s graveyard for having 0 or less toughness, persist won’t trigger and the card won’t return to the battlefield. That’s because persist checks the creature’s existence just before it leaves the battlefield, and it still has all those counters on it at that point.","oracle_id":"70cdd24a-8dc5-47b5-8729-9ebf486f4821","published_at":"2013-06-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a permanent has multiple instances of persist, they’ll each trigger separately, but the redundant instances will have no effect. If one instance returns the card to the battlefield, the next to resolve will do nothing.","oracle_id":"70cdd24a-8dc5-47b5-8729-9ebf486f4821","published_at":"2013-06-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a token with no -1/-1 counters on it has persist, the ability will trigger when the token is put into the graveyard. However, the token will cease to exist and can’t return to the battlefield.","oracle_id":"70cdd24a-8dc5-47b5-8729-9ebf486f4821","published_at":"2013-06-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If multiple creatures with persist are put into the graveyard at the same time (due to combat damage or a spell that destroys all creatures, for example), the active player (the player whose turn it is) puts all of their persist triggers on the stack in any order, then each other player in turn order does the same. The last trigger put on the stack is the first one that resolves. That means that in a two-player game, the nonactive player’s persist creatures will return to the battlefield first, then the active player’s persist creatures do the same. The creatures return to the battlefield one at a time.","oracle_id":"70cdd24a-8dc5-47b5-8729-9ebf486f4821","published_at":"2013-06-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The persist ability triggers when the permanent is put into a graveyard. Its last known information (that is, how the creature last existed on the battlefield) is used to determine whether it had a -1/-1 counter on it.","oracle_id":"70cdd24a-8dc5-47b5-8729-9ebf486f4821","published_at":"2013-06-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"When a permanent with persist returns to the battlefield, it’s a new object with no memory of or connection to its previous existence.","oracle_id":"70cdd24a-8dc5-47b5-8729-9ebf486f4821","published_at":"2013-06-07","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If there are fewer than twenty cards in the targeted player's library, that player puts all the cards from their library into their graveyard.","oracle_id":"cc2b6e58-2d6f-495e-95f3-9496105c4cba","published_at":"2009-10-01","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
